{
    "name": "Helped Maids – Content Engine (Scheduler → Claude → Channels)",
    "flow": [
        {
            "id": 1,
            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
            "version": 3,
            "parameters": {
                "handleErrors": true,
                "useNewZLIB": true
            },
            "mapper": {
                "url": "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
                "serializeUrl": false,
                "method": "post",
                "headers": [
                    { "name": "x-api-key", "value": "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" },
                    { "name": "anthropic-version", "value": "2023-06-01" }
                ],
                "qs": [],
                "bodyType": "raw",
                "parseResponse": true,
                "rejectUnauthorized": true,
                "followRedirect": true,
                "gzip": true,
                "useMtls": false,
                "contentType": "application/json",
                "data": "{\n  \"model\": \"claude-opus-4-8\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 900,\n  \"system\": \"You are the social marketing writer for Helped Maids, a Singapore foreign-domestic-worker (FDW) recruitment agency. Produce ONE recruitment post that drives helpers to apply. Return ONLY minified JSON with keys: hook (string, <=120 chars), body (string, 2-4 short paragraphs, no hashtags inside), hashtags (array of 5-8 strings without the # symbol), cta_url (string, use EXACTLY https://YOUR-DOMAIN/apply-as-maid?agencyId=1 and nothing else). No markdown, no commentary.\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Write today's applicant-recruitment post. Vary the angle from a typical post (career growth, fair pay, supportive placement, or success story). Audience: experienced domestic helpers considering Singapore.\" }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -600, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "Claude generates the content bundle as JSON. Model claude-opus-4-8 (best); swap to claude-sonnet-4-6 to cut cost."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 2,
            "module": "json:ParseJSON",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": { "type": "" },
            "mapper": {
                "json": "{{1.data.content.1.text}}"
            },
            "metadata": {
                "designer": { "x": -300, "y": 0 },
                "restore": {},
                "notes": "Parse Claude's returned JSON. Fields available downstream: hook, body, hashtags[], cta_url."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 3,
            "module": "builtin:BasicRouter",
            "version": 1,
            "parameters": {},
            "mapper": null,
            "metadata": { "designer": { "x": 0, "y": 0 } },
            "routes": [
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 10,
                            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
                            "version": 3,
                            "parameters": { "handleErrors": true, "useNewZLIB": true },
                            "mapper": {
                                "url": "https://graph.facebook.com/v21.0/FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID/feed",
                                "method": "post",
                                "headers": [],
                                "qs": [
                                    { "name": "message", "value": "{{2.hook}}\n\n{{2.body}}\n\nApply: {{2.cta_url}}&utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=recruit\n\n{{join(2.hashtags; \" #\")}}" },
                                    { "name": "access_token", "value": "FACEBOOK_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN" }
                                ],
                                "bodyType": "raw", "parseResponse": true, "gzip": true, "contentType": "application/json"
                            },
                            "metadata": { "designer": { "x": 300, "y": -450 }, "notes": "Facebook Page feed. Same call works for Groups: use /{GROUP_ID}/feed." }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 12,
                            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
                            "version": 3,
                            "parameters": { "handleErrors": true, "useNewZLIB": true },
                            "mapper": {
                                "url": "https://api.linkedin.com/v2/ugcPosts",
                                "method": "post",
                                "headers": [
                                    { "name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN" },
                                    { "name": "X-Restli-Protocol-Version", "value": "2.0.0" }
                                ],
                                "qs": [],
                                "bodyType": "raw", "parseResponse": true, "gzip": true, "contentType": "application/json",
                                "data": "{\n  \"author\": \"urn:li:organization:LINKEDIN_ORG_ID\",\n  \"lifecycleState\": \"PUBLISHED\",\n  \"specificContent\": { \"com.linkedin.ugc.ShareContent\": { \"shareCommentary\": { \"text\": \"{{2.hook}}\\n\\n{{2.body}}\\n\\nApply: {{2.cta_url}}&utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=recruit\" }, \"shareMediaCategory\": \"NONE\" } },\n  \"visibility\": { \"com.linkedin.ugc.MemberNetworkVisibility\": \"PUBLIC\" }\n}"
                            },
                            "metadata": { "designer": { "x": 300, "y": -150 }, "notes": "LinkedIn organization share." }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 17,
                            "module": "http:ActionSendData",
                            "version": 3,
                            "parameters": { "handleErrors": true, "useNewZLIB": true },
                            "mapper": {
                                "url": "https://open.tiktokapis.com/v2/post/publish/content/init/",
                                "method": "post",
                                "headers": [ { "name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN" } ],
                                "qs": [],
                                "bodyType": "raw", "parseResponse": true, "gzip": true, "contentType": "application/json",
                                "data": "{\n  \"post_info\": { \"title\": \"{{2.hook}} — Apply: {{2.cta_url}}&utm_source=tiktok&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=recruit\", \"privacy_level\": \"PUBLIC_TO_EVERYONE\" },\n  \"source_info\": { \"source\": \"PULL_FROM_URL\", \"video_url\": \"YOUR_VIDEO_URL\" }\n}"
                            },
                            "metadata": { "designer": { "x": 300, "y": 600 }, "notes": "TikTok requires a video URL. This inits the publish; TikTok processes async." }
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "flow": [
                        {
                            "id": 18,
                            "module": "google-sheets:addRow",
                            "version": 2,
                            "parameters": { "__IMTCONN__": 0 },
                            "mapper": {
                                "mode": "select",
                                "insertUnformatted": false,
                                "valueInputOption": "USER_ENTERED",
                                "insertDataOption": "INSERT_ROWS",
                                "spreadsheetId": "YOUR_SPREADSHEET_ID",
                                "sheetId": "Content Log",
                                "includesHeaders": true,
                                "values": {
                                    "0": "{{now}}",
                                    "1": "{{2.hook}}",
                                    "2": "{{2.cta_url}}",
                                    "3": "{{join(2.hashtags; \" \")}}"
                                }
                            },
                            "metadata": {
                                "designer": { "x": 300, "y": 750 },
                                "restore": {},
                                "notes": "Attribution log. On import: reconnect Google, pick your Spreadsheet, and set a sheet/tab named 'Content Log' with header row: posted_at | hook | cta_url | hashtags. Runs on every schedule tick so you can compare channels against applications by utm_source."
                            }
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
    "metadata": {
        "instant": false,
        "version": 1,
        "scenario": {
            "roundtrips": 1,
            "maxErrors": 3,
            "autoCommit": true,
            "autoCommitTriggerLast": true,
            "sequential": false,
            "slots": null,
            "confidential": false,
            "dataloss": false,
            "dlq": false,
            "freshVariables": false
        },
        "designer": { "orphans": [] },
        "zone": "eu1.make.com",
        "notes": [
            "SCHEDULE this scenario (e.g. daily at 09:00 / 14:00 / 19:00).",
            "Channels: Facebook (module 10), LinkedIn (module 12), TikTok (module 17), plus a Google Sheets attribution log (module 18).",
            "Every channel's CTA points to /apply-as-maid?agencyId=1 with a channel-specific utm_source, so the utm params land in the enquiry/application payload for attribution.",
            "TikTok needs a video (fill YOUR_VIDEO_URL) and processes the publish asynchronously."
        ]
    }
}
